💡 **SUGGESTION: Add `@visibleForTesting` to `activeApiKeyForTest` — the sibling convention is what enforces the documented test-only contract**

Every existing `xxxForTest` getter on `AgentService` (`toolsForTest`, `systemPromptForTest`, `secretsEnvForTest`, `redactorForTest`, …) carries `@visibleForTesting`; this new getter is the only one without it. The doc comment declares the contract ("test-only: no production reader — the key never surfaces in the UI"), but nothing enforces it — and unlike the other seams this one exposes a **credential** (`_activeApiKey`), which makes silent erosion of that contract more expensive than usual.

```dart
// flutter_app/lib/services/agent_service.dart:1390-1393
/// API key resolved into the active backend by [reconfigure] (test-only:
/// no production reader — the key never surfaces in the UI). Exposes the
/// preset-apply seam so widget tests can pin the bridged-key wiring.
String get activeApiKeyForTest => _activeApiKey;
```

Adding the annotation turns the documented invariant into an analyzer guard: any future production reader fails the build instead of shipping. Polish only — does not gate this merge.

